1500: actual source Tate chain and degree-zero line
1501: with gluing \(c=(QP)^a\), followed by the actual
1502: kernel contraction (SZ.45). This is the ordinary
1503: nonzero-line source filling under the explicit
1504: theta/Cartier map of Section 19. The E face and
1505: every H modification lie over \(v=0\).
1506: The finite-base pieces have the two literal deck
1507: squares (SZ.50)--(SZ.51) in their changed ordinary
1508: coordinate \(\eta\). The collision fan above uses
1509: the original Tate coordinate \(V\). Their common
1510: physical delta character is retained, but the
1511: coordinate change between these two central
1512: atlases still has to be extended. Its exact deck
1513: is recorded below.
1514: 
1515: This proves the local normal analytic collision
1516: quotient. Section 21 proves the finite-base partial
1517: attachment in its own chain coordinates. Their
1518: global central attachment is a separate remaining
1519: map. A
1520: period-equivariant toric resolution can subsequently
1521: be performed relative to the already smooth I,
1522: W and primitive E boundary subfans. Its new ray
1523: multiplicities must be retained. The resulting
1524: oriented boundary, the fixed-stratum incidence
1525: and the characteristic pairing have not been
1526: computed in this subsection; none is replaced
1527: by the determinant or fundamental-region count.
1528: 
1529: The base multiplicities are also literal. Since
1530: \(q_1-q_2=T_1(v)-T_0(v)=v\,u_v(v)\), with
1531: \(u_v(0)=4\), the I corner has
1532: \(q_1=xy,q_2=y\) and
1533: \(v=y(x-1)/u_v(v)\); the W corner has
1534: \(q_2=xy,q_1=y\) and
1535: \(v=y(1-x)/u_v(v)\). The E corner uses
1536: \(v=xy,q_1=y\). Thus an integral ray with
1537: base coordinates \((r,s)\) has \(v\)-order
1538: \(s,s,r+s\) in the I, W, E sectors respectively.
1539: These orders apply to the primitive integral
1540: rays of the actual refinement. They retain
1541: every higher H multiplicity. Each normal
1542: toric chart is the closure of its dense
1543: torus over the nonzero parameter, so no
1544: total-space component is contained in the
1545: central fibre, and its
1546: parameter function is a nonzero divisor.
1547: Its local rings are therefore torsion free
1548: over the one-dimensional parameter ring,
1549: which proves flatness of this local quotient over
1550: the \(v\)-disc.
1551: 
